      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "BACKGROUND",
          "content": "Step&Shoot cardiac computed tomography (CT) provides the benefit of significant reduction in radiation dose compared to helical cardiac CT acquisitions. We think that a difference occurs in image quality by presence of overlap reconstruction (fractionated sentence, attempted to clarify)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "PURPOSE",
          "content": "We studied the utility of Step&Shoot overlap reconstruction (SSOR)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "We evaluated image quality of SSOR by comparing z-axis spatial resolution on various s in scanners that SSOR is possible and for those that are impossible."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "SSOR indicated better z-axis spatial resolution and less variation over the field of view (FOV) (in z & x-y directions) as compared with Step&Shoot without overlap reconstruction (SS). In addition, SS showed inadequate image reproducibility due to aliasing error in z-direction (lack of sampling interval)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "content": "SSOR would contribute to improvement of the image quality of Step&Shoot cardiac CT."
        }
      ]},
